1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,720
We'll be heading along sun street because there is a rather interesting hotel to show you.
我们会沿 Sun Street 走，因为有一间挺有意思的旅馆想给你们看。

2
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:17,460
The sun hotel dating back to 1480 despite the 1503 plaque was once called the little inn.
作者说，Sun Hotel 可追溯至1480年，尽管铭牌写1503年；它曾叫 Little Inn。

3
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:21,240
And made famous by charles dickens in david copperfield.
它因查尔斯·狄更斯在《大卫·科波菲尔》中的描写而出名。

4
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:25,584
Dickens stayed here amongst other places during his visits to canterbury.
作者说，狄更斯来坎特伯雷时，除其他地方外也曾住在这里。

5
00:00:25,584 --> 00:00:32,720
A great fire in 1865 damaged timber buildings in the surrounding streets but luckily this one was virtually untouched.
1865年的大火损坏了周边街道的木结构建筑，但幸运的是，这一栋几乎没受影响。

6
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:43,320
We arrive at the well known butter market outside the cathedral by the christchurch gate where you enter the cathedral if visiting.
我们来到大教堂外著名的 Butter Market，在 Christchurch Gate 旁；参观教堂从那里进去。

7
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:51,680
Sadly it was completely covered in scaffolding we won't be visiting the cathedral in this video as due to covid we couldn't get one of the limited tickets.
可惜城门完全被脚手架遮住。这个视频不参观教堂，因为疫情期间没能买到限量门票。

8
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:54,320
But we'll put a link top right once we've been back.
不过等我们再去过，会在右上角放一个链接。

9
00:00:55,920 --> 00:01:06,230
Up until the 17 th century the butter market was known as the bull stake a place to tether bulls overnight to be baited by dogs believing it would produce more tender meat.
直到十七世纪，Butter Market 被称为 Bull Stake，是夜间拴公牛、让狗撕咬的地方，当时人认为这样肉更嫩。

10
00:01:06,230 --> 00:01:10,989
There are some incredibly old buildings and public houses in this area.
这片区域有一些年代非常久远的建筑和酒馆。

11
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:37,920
This shopping thoroughfare is burgate leading us to the city outer walls and where one of the eight gates to access the fortified city used to be.
这条商业通道是 Burgate，通向外城墙；过去进入设防城市的八座城门之一就在这里。

12
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:49,506
At various points you get glimpses of the cathedral but frustratingly it's hidden away from full view unless you have a ticket to enter the inner cathedral grounds.
沿途不时能瞥见教堂，但让人着急的是，很难看到全貌，除非有票进入教堂内院。

13
00:01:49,506 --> 00:01:56,737
Burgate meaning gate of the borough is actually one of only two street names in canterbury that are over a thousand years old.
Burgate 的意思是自治市之门；作者说，它是坎特伯雷仅有的两个超过千年的街名之一。

14
00:01:56,737 --> 00:02:07,840
The other is old ruttington lane look out for the moat tea room a tiny timber building with delightful looking cakes in the window.
另一个是 Old Ruttington Lane。留意 Moat Tea Room，一间小木结构屋，橱窗里蛋糕看起来很诱人。

15
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:17,840
Reaching the noisy main road the gate has gone but the city walls remain part of which date from roman times.
到了嘈杂的大路，城门已不在，城墙还在，其中部分可追溯到罗马时期。

16
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:32,891
Crossing the road we see a lone gatehouse in the distance we'll head up church street to explore this important area just outside the city walls.
过马路，远处有一座独立的门楼；我们沿 Church Street 往上，探索这片城墙外的重要区域。

17
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:48,165
This area holds the ruin of saint augustine's abbey founded in 598 a d.
这里有圣奥古斯丁修道院的遗迹，作者说它建于公元598年。

18
00:02:48,165 --> 00:02:54,320
After saint augustine arrived in kent on a mission to convert the pagan anglo saxons to christianity.
当时圣奥古斯丁来到肯特，使命是使信奉异教的盎格鲁撒克逊人改信基督教。

19
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:59,680
The work he began succeeded in converting the whole of England within a hundred years.
作者说，他开启的工作在一百年内成功使整个英格兰改信了基督教。

20
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:08,783
The abbey thrived and was dedicated to saint augustine in 978 it was one of the most important monasteries in medieval England.
修道院兴盛起来，978年奉献给圣奥古斯丁，是中世纪英格兰最重要的修道院之一。

21
00:03:08,783 --> 00:03:17,280
For almost 1000 years it was a centre of learning and spirituality until Henry viii had it torn down in the suppression of monasteries.
近一千年里，这里是学习和精神生活的中心，直到亨利八世在取缔修道院时下令拆毁。

22
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:25,160
What we see today is all that remains you can tour inside when open maintained by english heritage.
眼前就是仅存的部分。开放时可以入内参观，由 English Heritage 维护。
